      "selected_excerpts": [
        {
          "start_line": 3,
          "end_line": 6,
          "text": "**Verdict:** correspondence helped Gemma switch decisions within binary templates;\nselective three-option transfer failed. Qwen failed the frozen native competence\ngate, so fresh Qwen editing was **NOT MEASURED — UNQUALIFIED**, not a failed\nediting replication. STRONG CANDIDATE is false. No successor is authorized here."
        },
        {
          "start_line": 10,
          "end_line": 13,
          "text": "Independent units: **8 two-option families per domain; 4 three-option families\nper domain, a subset of those same families**. Each domain contributes 512 binary\nand 432 three-option decision rows. These are small authored, common-template\npopulations; the three-option task adds numeric ranking and an answer-interface"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 17,
          "end_line": 44,
          "text": "Destination-rule accuracy (%), Gemma post-block 27:\n\n| Task / domain | PAIRED | MEAN | Shuffled | Marginal | Random | Projected oracle | Full-state oracle | Direct instruction |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Two / allocation | 100.00 | 78.32 | 50.20 | 49.80 | 49.61 | 99.61 | 99.61 | 99.61 |\n| Two / reporting | 92.58 | 65.23 | 53.52 | 52.54 | 52.15 | 94.53 | 94.73 | 98.44 |\n| Three / allocation | 55.79 | **62.73** | 28.01 | 33.33 | 33.33 | 69.91 | 96.76 | 100.00 |\n| Three / reporting | 46.06 | 38.89 | 30.79 | 33.33 | 33.33 | 53.94 | 93.52 | 100.00 |\n\nPAIRED minus MEAN / SHUFFLED, percentage points; 97.5% paired family-bootstrap\nintervals, 4,000 draws, seed 260908:\n\n| Task / domain | Minus MEAN | Minus SHUFFLED |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Two / allocation | +21.68 [19.92, 23.24] | +49.80 [49.22, 50.00] |\n| Two / reporting | +27.34 [22.85, 31.25] | +39.06 [35.16, 42.38] |\n| Three / allocation | -6.94 [-10.42, -3.94] | +27.78 [23.61, 31.02] |\n| Three / reporting | +7.18 [5.56, 9.95] | +15.28 [12.96, 19.44] |\n\nPAIRED recognition / agreement harmful flips (% of **all corresponding rows**):\ntwo allocation 0 / 0; two reporting 2.54 / 0; three allocation 8.80 / 20.83;\nthree reporting 12.19 / 44.44. Net losses are reported separately. Secondary\nequal-domain accuracy is 96.29% binary and 50.93% three-option. The binary\nyardstick passes. Three-option accuracy, both preservation gates, mean advantage,\nits corrected lower bound, and allocation mean-advantage reversal (including\nswitch 0) fail. The allocation mean's stronger result belongs to that baseline.\n\n| Prespecified explanation | Disposition supported by this study |"
        },
        {
          "start_line": 56,
          "end_line": 64,
          "text": "All four Gemma primary maps selected rank 16 using old calibration only. The\noriginal 18 families were already exposed development (FIT 00–05, CAL 06–08),\nnot confirmation. No three-option fitting, favorable-case selection, layer\nsweep, backbone training or library upgrade occurred. Source-only updates use\nhidden state plus domain/requested switch; all 67,008 updates were frozen before\noracle access and reproduced exactly in live edit instrumentation. Projected,\nfull-state and cross-world oracles intentionally have counterfactual access;\nthey are diagnostics, not deployable competitors. Known low-rank ridge estimators\nwere used; this is not a new algorithm."
        }
      ]
    },
